hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1612","Narrated to us Salm ibn Junādah, narrated to us Wakīʿ, from Jaʿfar ibn Ḥayyān Abū al-Ashhab al-Saʿdī.\n\nAnd narrated to us Muḥammad ibn Maʿmar al-Qaysī, narrated to us Abū ʿĀmir, who informed us Abū al-Ashhab, who narrated to us Abū Naḍrah, from Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī (RA), who said:\nThe Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ) saw some delay in his Companions (RA), so he said:\n\"Move forward, follow my lead, and let those who come after you follow your lead. The people will continue to fall behind until Allāh causes them to fall behind.\"\n\nThis is the narration of Wakīʿ.\n\nIbn Maʿmar said: \"From Abū Naḍrah al-ʿAbdī.\"\n\n---\n**CHAPTER:**"
